<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buhen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buhen was an Egyptian fortress and settlement on the west bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> near the Second Cataract, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-nubia">Lower Nubia</a>. Built in its massive form under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senusret-i">Senusret I</a>, with mud-brick walls, bastions and a ditch, it controlled the river frontier with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> and was reused in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>. Excavated in the 1950s and 1960s, it was then flooded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-nasser">Lake Nasser</a> behind the Aswan High Dam.</p></div>
